.TH LUMART 1 "September 2026" "Lumart 2.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lumart, luma \- High-Fidelity Terminal Visual Suite (Mary Apex, Trumble Orelx, Luris Mono, Spectra Weep)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lumart
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIIMAGE_PATH_OR_URL\fR]
.br
.B luma
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIIMAGE_PATH_OR_URL\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlumart\fR is an industrial-grade terminal image and video renderer designed for high-definition visual fidelity in modern terminal emulators. Powered by C++17 OpenMP SIMD routines and Python OpenCV acceleration, Lumart projects raster graphics, vector animations, manga screentones, and real-time webcam video feeds directly into standard ANSI/Unicode text viewports.

Lumart routes inputs across four flagship rendering engines:
.TP
.B Mary Apex 3.5
Photorealistic vector TrueColor engine using the \fBOklab perceptual color space\fR, discrete 31-partition combinatorial optimization per sextant cell, and SIMD-accelerated C++17.
.TP
.B Trumble Orelx 2.2
Capcom CPS-2 retro-arcade cel-shading engine featuring \fB1-to-1 subpixel Canny edge detection\fR, Retinex multi-scale contrast, and vibrant comic punch.
.TP
.B Luris Mono 2.6
Japanese manga screentone and line-art engine utilizing \fB8x8 Bayer halftone matrices\fR, adaptive Difference-of-Gaussians (DoG) edge filters, and transparent background PNG sticker generation.
.TP
.B Spectra Weep 1.4
Hardware-accelerated real-time video and webcam streaming engine operating at 30\(en60 FPS with live terminal shader matrix filters.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS "Engine Selection"
.TP
\fB\-E\fR, \fB\-\-engine\fR \fIENGINE\fR
Explicitly select the rendering engine. Supported values: \fBmary\fR, \fBtrumble\fR, \fBluris\fR, \fBspectra\fR. By default, Lumart automatically routes based on options and content.

.SS "Subpixel Textures & Halftones"
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-sextants\fR
Render using Unicode 2\(mu3 Sextant characters (U+1FB00\(enU+1FB3B). Default for Mary Apex. Yields 6 subpixels per cell with independent foreground and background colors.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-braille\fR
Render using Unicode 2\(mu4 Braille patterns (U+2800\(enU+28FF). Yields 8 subpixels per character cell, ideal for fine stippling and detailed sketches.
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-quadrants\fR
Render using Unicode 2\(mu2 Quadrant block characters (4 subpixels per cell).
.TP
\fB\-\-blocks\fR
Render using optimized half-block characters (\(ua / \(da) with independent foreground and background colors.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-manga\fR
Activate Manga Screentone 2.0 mode (Bayer 8\(mu8 matrix dithering combined with adaptive DoG vector ink outlines).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-sketch\fR
Activate clean line sketch mode without screentone dithering.

.SS "Viewport, Geometry & Dimensions"
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR
Set explicit output width in terminal character columns. Incompatible with \fB\-F\fR / \fB\-\-fit\fR.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-fit\fR
\fBAuto-fit to terminal viewport\fR: dynamically queries terminal rows and columns, calculating the optimal bounding box to render the image without vertical scrolling. Incompatible with \fB\-w\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-ratio\fR \fIRATIO\fR
Calibrate terminal font width-to-height aspect ratio (default: \fB0.5\fR). Adjust to \fB0.45\fR\(en\fB0.48\fR for tall fonts (Fira Code) or \fB0.52\fR\(en\fB0.58\fR for wide fonts.
.TP
\fB\-\-fastfetch\fR, \fB\-\-logo\fR
Auto-crop transparent and empty bounding margins for seamless inclusion in Fastfetch or Neofetch sidebars.

.SS "Color, Tone & Palette"
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-color\fR
Force TrueColor (24-bit RGB) ANSI rendering (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable color escape sequences and route to monochrome pipeline.
.TP
\fB\-\-boost\fR, \fB\-\-vibrant\fR
Apply Retinex multi-scale dynamic range compression, boosting saturation and contrast for arcade-style vibrancy.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-invert\fR
Invert luminance values (useful for light terminal backgrounds; automatically detected in \fB\-m\fR).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dither\fR [\fIALGORITHM\fR]
Select error-diffusion algorithm: \fBatkinson\fR (default), \fBfloyd\fR, \fBbayer\fR, or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-swap\fR \fICOLOR1\fR \fICOLOR2\fR
Dynamically swap colors within 3D RGB Euclidean color space.

.SS "Image Export & Animations"
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-\-save\fR \fIFILE\fR
Rasterize the terminal render to an image file (\fB.png\fR, \fB.jpg\fR) or compiled animated GIF (\fB.gif\fR). Note: WebP export is permanently deprecated.
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\fR
\fBAnimation mode\fR: caches decoded frames in memory for smooth 60 FPS terminal playback, or compiles an animated input into a subpixel GIF when combined with \fB\-o output.gif\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-transparent\fR
\fBLuris Mono exclusive\fR: exports manga renders as alpha-transparent PNG stickers (over 90% true transparency).
.TP
\fB\-\-instant\fR, \fB\-\-no\-reveal\fR
Display render output immediately without progressive line scanning (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-reveal\fR
Enable theatrical progressive top-to-bottom scanline animation.
.TP
\fB\-\-paste\fR
Grab image data directly from system clipboard and render immediately.

.SS "System Utilities & Lifecycle"
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-webcam\fR [\fICAMERA_INDEX\fR]
Launch real-time webcam terminal stream at 30\(en60 FPS (default index: 0).
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fICODE\fR
Set interface language (\fBen\fR, \fBes\fR, \fBpt\fR, \fBfr\fR, \fBru\fR, \fBja\fR, \fBde\fR, \fBko\fR).
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-history\fR [\fIN\fR]
Display last N executed commands from persistent command history.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-replay\fR [\fIN\fR]
Re-run the N-th command from history (default: last command).
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-history\fR
Wipe all command history from \fI~/.config/luma/history\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-desktop\fR
Install desktop integration and file manager context menu entry ("Open with Lumart") for Nautilus, Dolphin, Nemo, and Thunar.
.TP
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell tab-completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, or \fBfish\fR.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display minimalist diagnostic card detailing hardware architecture, OS, Python version, C++ compiler, SIMD/OpenMP support, and shared library health.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\fR, \fB\-\-check\-update\fR
Query GitHub API for available upstream updates.
.TP
\fB\-uu\fR, \fB\-\-upgrade\fR
Perform automated in-place upgrade to latest upstream release.
.TP
\fB\-dg\fR, \fB\-\-downgrade\fR [\fIVERSION\fR]
Interactive or direct rollback to previously installed version or specific release.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
General runtime error (file not found, invalid URL, unreadable image).
.TP
.B 2
CLI argument validation error or mutually exclusive flag conflict (e.g. \fB\-\-fit\fR combined with \fB\-\-width\fR).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma/history
Command execution history log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma/backup/
Backup archives for version rollback.
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma/settings.json
User preferences (language, default flags).

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Render image to full terminal width in photorealistic TrueColor (zero-flag default):
.RS
.B lumart photo.jpg
.RE
.PP
Auto-fit image perfectly to terminal viewport without scrolling:
.RS
.B lumart artwork.png \-F
.RE
.PP
Apply Capcom CPS-2 retro-arcade cel-shading with vibrant Retinex boost:
.RS
.B lumart sprite.png \-E trumble \-\-blocks \-\-boost
.RE
.PP
Render Japanese manga screentone and export as transparent PNG sticker:
.RS
.B lumart character.png \-m \-\-transparent \-o sticker.png
.RE
.PP
Play animated GIF in terminal loop at 60 FPS:
.RS
.B lumart animation.gif \-\-loop
.RE
.PP
Compile animated input into high-resolution animated GIF:
.RS
.B lumart animation.gif \-\-loop \-o output.gif
.RE
.PP
Generate Bash completions:
.RS
.B eval "$(lumart \-\-completions bash)"
.RE

